---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/site-layout.astro';
import Bird from '../assets/bird.svg';
---

<SiteLayout title="Playground · Birdie" description="A planned WebAssembly playground for writing and running Birdie in the browser.">
  <section class="play-intro wrap" aria-labelledby="play-heading">
    <h1 id="play-heading">Browser<br />playground.</h1>
    <p>The planned playground will run Birdie locally in your browser using WebAssembly.</p>
    <div class="play-placeholder">
      <Bird width={100} height={106} aria-hidden="true" />
      <div>
        <h2>This bird isn’t flying just yet.</h2>
        <p>The interpreter needs to be built first. For now, the examples have Birdie and Python versions you can compare using the code tabs.</p>
        <a class="button button-primary" href="/docs/examples/">Read the examples <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <a class="text-link" href="/docs/roadmap/">Interpreter and playground plans <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
